From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: apss-ipq6018: detour the IPQ5018 CPU through GPLL0 on a rate change

The IPQ53xx SoCs register a notifier that parks the CPU mux on GPLL0
for the length of a CPU PLL rate change, because their Stromer Plus PLL
stops its output while it relocks. The IPQ50xx ones do not. Their PLL
only takes a new rate when it is relocked from reset as well (0975), so
without the detour a rate change would stop the clock the CPU is
running from. This is why IPQ5018 has had a single operating point
(0912).

Register the same notifier for the IPQ50xx SoC IDs.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/apss-ipq6018.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/apss-ipq6018.c
@@ -132,6 +132,18 @@
 	case QCOM_ID_IPQ5332:
 	case QCOM_ID_IPQ5322:
 	case QCOM_ID_IPQ5300:
+	/*
+	 * The IPQ50xx CPU PLL is relocked from reset on a rate change,
+	 * which stops its output, so it needs the same detour through
+	 * GPLL0.
+	 */
+	case QCOM_ID_IPQ5000:
+	case QCOM_ID_IPQ5010:
+	case QCOM_ID_IPQ5016:
+	case QCOM_ID_IPQ5018:
+	case QCOM_ID_IPQ5028:
+	case QCOM_ID_IPQ0509:
+	case QCOM_ID_IPQ0518:
 		cpu_clk_notifier = devm_kzalloc(&pdev->dev,
 						sizeof(*cpu_clk_notifier),
 						GFP_KERNEL);
